    "attributes": {
        "action": "Extend the bus fare cap in England to trams",
        "additional_details": "Comparison of UK tram single fares as of 27th July 2026, not covered by the bus fare cap: \r\nBirmingham between \u00a32.50 and \u00a35.30; \r\nBlackpool \u00a33 or \u00a33.50; \r\nManchester between \u00a31.40 and \u00a34.80; \r\nNottingham \u00a33.60;\r\nSheffield \u00a32.50 or \u00a33",
        "background": "We call upon the Government to extend the England bus fare cap to trams.\r\nTrams have often regenerated deprived neighbourhoods, yet bus services often reduce as a result, so poor neighbourhoods are left with little choice but to get the more expensive tram. There should be a level playing field.",
